> An idea for a sound warning, maybe "You hear men singing" or just "Yo ho ho
> and a bottle of rum"

Cool, cool.  Maybe seagulls would work as well.

The only problem I could see is that these sounds would be less
appropriate if the moat were full of lava instead of water.  I don't
know how easy it would be to distinguish between the two in the noise
code, since they're both the same "kind" of room.  While water isn't
deadly unless the player cannot make it back to shore, lava is
instantly fatal if blundered into without fire resistance, so I'd
think that would be the more imperative case for a warning message.

By the way, if people decide to play with this patch I'd be grateful
if they'd report on how it changes the game for them, and if it's
positive or not.  As it is the room is fairly rare.  (You can test it
out by setting SHOPTYPE to W and playing in wizard mode, but this also
disables the level check for blocking rooms.)

The worst thing about the patch is that the island can block progress
starting on level 5.  The player is free to go back to the Gnomish
Mines at that point and get a pick-axe in order to proceed, but some
classes have trouble with the mines that early.

The second-worst thing about it is that, being yet another type of
special room and there can only be one on a random level at this time,
its existence makes other types of special rooms marginally less
common.

The best thing about the patch is that it makes wands of fire and ice,
scrolls of earth, boots of levitation and jumping, and knights more
useful.  Maybe other things too -- what other ways are there to get
across water?  Across lava?  It also makes gold a little more common,
but the room shows up rarely enough that I doubt that'll be a big
problem.

